WEBVTT

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.590
A castle of arrogance towering over a city of vanity...

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:04.960
Or is it the reckless lance of the ignorant?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.140
We're here.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.610
I hate to say it when you're waxing poetic, but we're going.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.050
Right.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:37.590
So this is it. This is a magnificent sight.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:42.440
In order for the phase shift caused by the Aharonov-Bohm effect...

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.780
...to affect the gauge field of the entire Settlement, something this size is necessary.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.920
That's fine with us,

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.450
...since at this point, construction of the tower is our top priority.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.330
What concerns the Chairman though,

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.990
...is the delay in the construction schedule.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.330
If so, then I'd like you to do something about those terrorists.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.570
Trains and trucks carrying building materials...

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.100
...have been attacked five times already.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.780
For that, I think contracting with that firm would be best.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.180
Perhaps that displeases you, Doctor, but...

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.020
Dr. Enuma!

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.490
You have a telephone call.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.990
From whom?

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.930
From a woman named Kageyama.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.060
Kageyama?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.030
It couldn't be!

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.400
Excuse me for a moment.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.430
Yes, Enuma here.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:58.680
It was you after all! This brings back memories, Hiroko Kageyama.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:04.080
I haven't been called by that name in a long time, Dr. Enuma.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.390
I've heard various rumors about you.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.860
What? You'll lend me a hand for old times' sake?

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.400
I see. You seem to know a lot about it.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.270
But there are things we can't tell outsiders.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.810
I appreciate the offer though.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.530
Well then, what time would be best for you?

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.540
<i>Hey!</i>

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.070
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.030
<i>What's that?</i>

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.790
<i>Nice catch!</i>

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.100
<i>Well, Madoka, how do you like your first time in the Core Settlement?</i>

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.800
It's no big deal.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.940
<i>Talking tough, huh?</i>

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.080
<i>I'll bet last night you were so excited you couldn't sleep.</i>

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.690
<i>No way!</i>

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.660
<i>But this town does have a floaty feeling to it.</i>

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:53.700
<i>What do you mean, floaty?</i>

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.600
<i>That's because it's a typical company town,</i>

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.000
<i>...a papier-mache city built using Mitleid's corporate prestige.</i>

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.810
<i>The sky's the same as everywhere else though.</i>

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.420
<i>Fu, that's too much fooling around!</i>

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.920
<i>Don't be so uptight!</i>

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.700
Don't cut loose too much just because you're in the Settlement.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.710
You're not there for pleasure.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.050
Whatever you say!

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.480
Tatsuya, you understand, right?

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.820
Huh? Uh, yes, Ma'am.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:50.880
Not about that, I mean about when you encounter members of Gilgamesh.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.250
Oh...

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.390
I don't want to force you to do anything.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.930
If you think you're in danger, get away immediately.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.470
<i>Tatsuya, it's coming your way!</i>

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:08.840
<i>Okay!</i>

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.110
<i>It's fine. Madoka has gotten good at this now, like us.</i>

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.610
<i>His Dynamis has gotten stronger too.</i>

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:19.550
<i>Although until just recently, he was hopelessly bummed out.</i>

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.550
<i>I hope he doesn't get carried away and screw up.</i>

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.300
Ah!

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.200
This is so cool! It's that game they used to have!

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.790
It's back out again!

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.970
What's that about? She's the one fooling around!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:43.270
<i>I can hear you! I never get carried away or anything! Unlike you!</i>

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.640
I don't let my guard down either!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.760
Loser!

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.360
We've got the general features of the town in our heads.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.920
Let's get going.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.520
'Bye.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:24.540
It's fortunate, Dr. Enuma, that you had taken that fellowship with Mitleid.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:31.620
Some researchers from Heaven's Gate kept working by moving right over to this firm.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.690
Quite a number of them.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:42.090
As for me, Dr. Kageyama, I want to see that blue sky once more.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.270
Since that day fifteen years ago,

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.930
...the world has been covered by an accursed mirror,

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:51.330
...and we've been tossed into a whirlpool of chaos.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:57.020
Though all we lost were all the computers on the face of the Earth...

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.180
...and long-distance wireless communications.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.990
To the network-dependent society of the time,

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.510
...it was a fatal wound.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.890
People everywhere joined together in blaming us at Heaven's Gate,

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:13.690
...saying our mysterious research had triggered this atrocity.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.060
But in the end, it became known that it was the act of a lone terrorist.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:25.180
Unlike you and the others, I was away from Uruk at the time,

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:27.610
...so I don't truly know what happened.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.370
For me, that sky alone is the loathsome enemy.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.940
I recall that at that time, you were...

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.880
I've finally managed to get this far.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.420
I won't let anyone stand in my way.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.550
It seems they're here.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.320
Huh?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.170
Come in.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.900
These children are the ones?

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.340
I see.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:10.520
Your faces bring back memories, all of you.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.230
Shall we move into our main topic?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:23.330
This thing you're constructing in the guise of a new office building,

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:28.830
...the thing Gilgamesh is interfering with by going as far as causing explosions...

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.010
What on earth is it?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.610
A magic staff to return the world to what it was.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.720
It looks like you, perceptive as ever, had guessed that already.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.890
Very well, I'll show it to you...

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:50.550
Our Turangalila.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.490
Turangalila?

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:07.350
A geomagnetic abnormality was the cause of the world's chaos,

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.410
...and the Sheltering Sky was no more than a visible manifestation of it.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.080
That's what we thought for a long time.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:17.650
But that was a one-sided understanding.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:32.470
The correct answer is that cosmic rays, incessantly pouring down,

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:35.010
...are colliding with the electrically-charged atmosphere...

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.640
...as they pass through the Sheltering Sky,

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:41.200
...creating an abnormal magnetic field in the ionosphere that hangs over us like a curtain.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.310
A Dellinger effect.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.080
Right, and on a worldwide scale.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:50.050
It's as if the sky has an electromagnetic-field umbrella.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:01.200
So in effect, to correct this abnormality,

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.270
...one would have to correct the geomagnetic abnormality...

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.600
...and the abnormality in the sky at the same time.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:10.240
We will heal both Heaven and Earth at the same time,

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:13.230
...and the magic staff for it is this tower.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.880
Okay, look this way.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.390
This is a pain in the butt.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.200
It's all the same to us, having some ID card or not having it.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:35.970
It's not about what we need.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:39.460
It's so they can distinguish us from THEM.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.510
I always look terrible in these kinds of pictures.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.780
Your face looks like a criminal's?

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.280
Yeah, yeah, like a convict.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:55.040
I wonder how that Enuma lady and the Countess know each other?

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.610
Who knows? Seems like they're acquaintances from before Twin X.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:02.460
I get the feeling they're not such good friends, huh?

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.360
Then again,

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.990
...that woman doesn't seem to have any good friends or anything.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.290
It's amazing though.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.600
What is?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:16.200
I never even thought that there might be people seriously trying to get rid of that sky.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.470
People who knew the old sky are desperate for it.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:23.870
For us, the sky has been like this since the time we were born.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.020
Yeah, you're right.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.680
We just think, like, it's fine if it stays this way.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.510
But it is amazing.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.900
What's this?

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:43.130
It's an anti-electron-neutrino generator.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:48.540
You mean you want to use this to regulate the atmospheric neutrino balance.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:53.840
The underground vector potential regulator will even out the geomagnetic abnormality,

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:58.840
...and we will irradiate the sky with anti-electron-neutrinos generated here.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.220
If all goes well,

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.550
...we can get back a world uninfluenced by the Sheltering Sky,

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.990
...though only in approximately a 20-km radius.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:10.350
I'm impressed you could build this sort of thing.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.160
"Without computers," you want to say, right?

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.300
We have a computer.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.900
What?

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:27.480
In theory, it only takes a device that can perform operations with ones and zeroes, right?

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.380
That being so, one could even use vacuum tubes,

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.540
...which are unaffected by the Sheltering Sky.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:49.360
This entire floor is one giant vacuum-tube computer.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:55.400
With this we can cover everything from designing systems to managing them.

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.640
Of course, once the blue sky comes back, all this can be replaced...

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.640
...by one of the laptop computers we used in the old days.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:11.750
But if this place is targeted, this whole plan will come to naught.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:16.060
They can't enter here.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:17.520
What?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:22.070
More accurately, nobody can teleport inside these walls,

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.730
...because Dynamis won't work.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.940
That's why that bunch is targeting our materials shipments and such,

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.500
...rather than striking here directly.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:35.170
Dynamis won't work? These walls couldn't be...

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:39.980
They are. We used Warka lapis stone from Uruk,

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.550
...in all the outer walls.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.750
I'm impressed you got so much. That's certainly a show of power.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.190
It's very like your company to do that.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:53.620
Or rather, perhaps I should say, very like that old gentleman.

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:58.630
Having you as an ally would undoubtedly please him.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.870
What he's trying to do is a bit different from my goals.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.040
And from yours.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:08.880
That's right.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:31.070
The first time I came to the Settlement I was thinking.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.300
Thinking what?

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:34.770
I thought it was somehow like a different world.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.240
So you WERE like a country boy seeing the sights!

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.710
How can I say it?

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.840
I felt like the power of humanity isn't totally lost.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:45.940
Because until now I only knew what life was like in a local town.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.380
The same with living at the Hotel Providence.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:53.750
I felt like, "So there's this world too."

00:16:54.260 --> 00:17:00.900
Yeah, I understand that a little, since we all lived a lot like you...

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.800
...until we were picked up by the Countess.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.990
And now there are these people building that kind of tower.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.030
Before, I spent my life just running away,

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.440
...but I wondered a little if that was good enough.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.140
Tatsuya, you've changed.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:18.350
Huh?

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.410
You've become tougher, somehow.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.380
But I'm not sure you need to think so seriously about it.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:27.520
Yeah, yeah. That kind of talk is, like, so lame.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.700
What is it?

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.230
They're here.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.470
<i>This is a roundabout way of doing things.</i>

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.440
<i>Don't say that.</i>

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:46.080
<i>If we can come away with a big picture of their plans,</i>

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.940
<i>...what follows will be easy.</i>

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:06.830
What do you think? That's the big picture of the October Project.

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.330
October?

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.700
Yes, its operational test will be on October 10th.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.260
That's the date of Twin X.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:24.170
Now it's your turn. Gilgamesh's power exceeds what we imagined.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:27.480
How do we counter them?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.410
<i>Countess, are you there?</i>

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:31.650
<i>Toru?</i>

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:35.690
<i>I finally got through to you! They're here! Do we drive them off?</i>

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.290
<i>How many of them are here?</i>

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:43.060
<i>One, two, probably three. We can do it!</i>

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.530
What's wrong?

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:52.080
Very well, now we'll show you something.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:57.540
<i>Toru, do you know their location?</i>

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:01.280
<i>Wait, they keep jumping.</i>

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.390
<i>They're headed upward!</i>

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:06.190
<i>They intend to destroy the hub of the company headquarters.</i>

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.260
<i>Stop them!</i>

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.220
I'll go first.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.530
<i>Toru, let's attack them from both sides.</i>

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.100
<i>Madoka, you're with Fu.</i>

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.360
Don't slow me down, okay?

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:26.510
<i>Tatsuya, you understand what I said yesterday, right?</i>

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.650
Yes!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:34.920
<i>Something's here.</i>

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.390
<i>What something?</i>

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.480
<i>Something sinister.</i>

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:45.860
Oh! So it's just these kids, is it?

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:12.380
<i>Let's lure them out into town!</i>

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.660
<i>Our plan has been upset. It seems that kid is here.</i>

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:49.560
<i>Madoka?!</i>

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:51.950
Yeah...

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.430
<i>Are you scared?</i>

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.920
Not at all!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:56.660
<i>They're over here.</i>

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.970
Nobody here!

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.650
What?

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:33.760
Hi...

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.180
They say a few years after Twin X,

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:30.390
...children were born with paranormal powers around the world.

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:33.190
In any case, I got to see a lot of faces from the past today.

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:35.290
They were called superiors,

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:37.960
...and were talked about as a portent, even, of a new evolution.

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:40.590
If only I had kids like those around me all the time...

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.630
I suppose it was for the sake of fighting against Enkidu.

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:43.800
Actually, I also should have...

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:45.470
I'm a bit jealous of you.

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:46.540
Those children are different!

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:47.670
Quite impressive that you located them.

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:49.070
Apparently the children are fine.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:51.730
That's why this is revenge for me,

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:53.800
...revenge on that sky.
